* ===========================================================================
* fBlockKit -- OpenMolcas magnetic-property chain (input generation only)
* title: {{ title }}
* Source skeleton and line annotations: {{ source_note }}
* Spin blocks: {{ spin_block_summary }}
* Active space: {{ nactel }} electrons in {{ nactorb }} orbitals; molecular charge {{ charge }}
* Basis assignment to write into {{ coord_file }}:
*   {{ element }} = {{ basis_metal }};
*   first coordination sphere = {{ basis_ligand }};
*   all remaining atoms = {{ basis_outer }}
* ===========================================================================
* Notes added by fBlockKit (tags [fBlockKit:...]) -- the source input has none of them:
*   [fBlockKit:G3-1] Comment character: "*" at the start of a line is the documented
*     OpenMolcas comment marker (documentation users.guide/emil.html, checked 2026-09-25);
*     comments may not sit between a keyword and its continuation lines. This file keeps
*     every comment on its own line. If your version still rejects these lines, delete
*     every line that starts with "*".
*   [fBlockKit:G3-7] The source's 28 line annotations are placed here on the lines the
*     internal close-reading aligns them to; that alignment is an inference from the
*     source's printed order, not a printed fact.
*   [fBlockKit:G3-4] Blocks are written in decreasing spin multiplicity and each block
*     after the first reads the previous block's orbital file (Typeindex / FILEORB);
*     this follows the source's example order, which the source does not state as a rule.
*   [fBlockKit:G3-5] The &SINGLE_ANISO sampling parameters below are the source's values;
*     they are not exposed as options in this version -- edit them in place if your
*     experiment needs different temperature or field grids.
* ===========================================================================

&GATEWAY
* Set up integral options
    AMFI
* Calculate SOC integrals
    RICD=acCD
* Use RI approximation
    Coord= {{ coord_file }}
* Define structure and basis (one file holds the geometry and the per-atom basis)
*
* [fBlockKit] Per-atom basis labels expected in that file:
*   {{ element }} : {{ basis_metal }}
*   first coordination sphere : {{ basis_ligand }}
*   all remaining atoms : {{ basis_outer }}
    Angmom= {{ angmom_origin }} ANGSTROM
* Set origin for angmom
*
* [fBlockKit:G3-3] The point group below is the one this job was generated with
*   (default C1 = no symmetry). The source example writes "group= NoSym" instead;
*   confirm which spelling your version accepts.
    group= {{ symmetry }}
* Don't use symmetry

&SEWARD
* Calculate integrals

{% for block in blocks %}
&RASSCF
{% if block.first %}
* Spin multiplicity
    Spin= {{ block.spin }}
* Molecular charge
    Charge= {{ charge }}
* Num roots (twice), unity weighting
    CiRoot= {{ block.nroots }} {{ block.nroots }} 1
* Num active electrons
    Nactel= {{ nactel }} 0 0
* Num active orbitals
    RAS2= {{ nactorb }}
{% else %}
* Read type of orbitals from file
    Typeindex
* Spin multiplicity
    Spin= {{ block.spin }}
* Molecular charge
    Charge= {{ charge }}
* Take starting MOs from here
    FILEORB= {{ block.prev_rasorb }}
* Num roots (twice), unity weighting
    CiRoot= {{ block.nroots }} {{ block.nroots }} 1
* Num active electrons
    Nactel= {{ nactel }} 0 0
{% endif %}
* Copy IPH file
>> COPY $Project.JobIph {{ block.iph }}
* Copy rasscf.h5 file
>> COPY $Project.rasscf.h5 {{ block.h5 }}
{% if block.next_rasorb %}
* [fBlockKit:G3-2] Addition not shown in the source: the next block reads
*   FILEORB= {{ block.next_rasorb }}, so this block's orbital file is copied to that name.
*   Verify the source file name ($Project.RasOrb) in your version, or delete this line
*   if the file is already produced under that name.
>> COPY $Project.RasOrb {{ block.next_rasorb }}
{% endif %}

{% endfor %}
* [fBlockKit:G3-8] "Nactel=" / "RAS2=" / "CiRoot=" spellings and the meaning of the three
*   numbers after Nactel are reproduced verbatim from the source example; they were not
*   cross-checked against the OpenMolcas documentation for this version.
*   As in the source, only the first block carries RAS2=; the later blocks take the
*   orbital types from the file they read.

&RASSI
* Calculate SOC elements
    SPIN
* Print matrix elements
    MEES
* Calculate g-values
    EPRG= {{ rassi_eprg }}
* Num multiplicities, which roots
    Nr of JobIph= {{ blocks | length }} ALL
* Names of IPH files
    IPHN
{% for block in blocks %}
    {{ block.iph }}
{% endfor %}
* Print angmom matrix elements
* [fBlockKit:G3-6] The source asks for one 'ANGMOM' property per spin block (three blocks
*   there); this file asks for {{ blocks | length }}, one per block, by the same pattern.
    PROP
    {{ blocks | length }}
{% for block in blocks %}
    'ANGMOM' {{ block.index }}
{% endfor %}

&SINGLE_ANISO
* Set angular momenta
    CRYS= {{ element_lower }}
* Ground state is a doublet
* [fBlockKit] The source's annotation for this line is "Ground state is a doublet"; the
*   numbering convention of MLTP is not stated there -- check it against your output.
    MLTP= {{ single_aniso_mltp }}
* Temperatures for susceptibility
    TINT= {{ single_aniso_tint }}
* Fields for magnetisation
    HINT= {{ single_aniso_hint }}
* Temperature for magnetisation
    TMAG= {{ single_aniso_tmag }}
* Quantisation axis from ground KD
    QUAX= {{ single_aniso_quax }}
